ID: vr-13
Title: Local desktop shell, transparent head overlay, cursor gaze and XYZ orientation
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Verona/issues/12

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Run Verona as a local desktop app and pop the same speaking head over other applications.
Dependencies: vr-12

Purpose:
Provide a genuinely transparent desktop background, rather than only a
transparent-looking face material. Preserve one clip, audio clock and renderer.

Tasks:
[x] Add a pinned, isolated desktop runtime and explicit setup/launch commands.
[x] Implement transparent always-on-top pop-out and return-to-controls without reloading.
[x] Add cursor-following eyes and independent full-range XYZ rotation/reset.
[x] Exercise actual native windows, alpha composition, speech continuity and recovery.
[ ] Update book, guide, ownership/failure evidence, issue/Project and continuity.
[ ] Review, commit and push coherent verified milestones as Zanark.

Acceptance criteria:
The overlay visibly composites over a synthetic desktop window. Controls return
without losing input, voice, clip or playback position. Cursor gaze works outside
the app without recording mouse input. All three axes span a full revolution.
Existing local-only browser mode remains operational; no device activation,
global installation, startup service or disturbance of other applications.

Completion evidence:
Implemented and environment-qualified, not yet source-published. Framework choice
reuses existing WebGL/audio with a pinned official Electron desktop compositor;
larger than WebView2, but avoids unproven layered-HWND transparency and duplicate
renderers/audio ownership. Windows desktop toolchains and existing runtime
processes inspected: no active Verona instance before edits.
35 unit/HTTP checks and focused XYZ/gaze math pass. Native desktop-overlay-10
passes 8 actual checks, including Windows composition over an owned green
fixture, outside-window gaze, full XYZ, uninterrupted single audio and return.
30-second native cadence: 1801 intervals, mean16.659ms/p9516.8/max17.8,
zero>25ms and1831actual draws at480x600. Not GPU timing or universal60fps.
Actual production entry point launcher-01: visible/responsive native window,
WM_CLOSE returns0, observed temporary profile removed. Native images reviewed.
Final browser05 passes20scenarios and six density/material modes; every mode
zero new normal GPU-buffer storage allocations and185-187actual updates.
Means16.659-17.184ms/p95atmost16.9/max66.7,nineintervals>25ms.
Mean/p95 budget passes; residual outliers remain, not locked60fps.
Historical browser02/03 mean-budget failures retained; cause not established.
New reusable CPU scratch/two preallocated dynamic normal buffers remove churn.
Separate desktop media provenance preserves the older vr12 capture snapshot.
Muted playback is not listening/phonetic acceptance; gaze is procedural.
Focused host regression covers explicit recovery and nonzero fatal exits;
fatal native errors must not return success to the Python owner/launcher.
Native07-09 pin failures retained; owned fixture probes of realWS_EX_TOPMOST
verified explicit pop-up-menu level, not unreliable default/floating. This
documented level is above the Windows taskbar; checkbox off/Controls unpins.

